# Cloudflare Pages headers. Committed, no build.
#
# EVERYTHING REVALIDATES, NOTHING SITS AT THE EDGE. Measured 2026-09-21: a deploy that changed one
# module reported success, curl fetched the new bytes, and every browser at the MCI edge kept getting
# the OLD module for a further twelve minutes and counting -- because a module import is a CORS
# request with an Origin header, Cloudflare keys that variant separately, and the deploy's purge did
# not reach it. This site is a few hundred small files whose whole point is that what was deployed is
# what you get, so the edge is told not to keep any of it and browsers are told to ask every time
# (an ETag round-trip, 304 if unchanged). bin/deploy's post-check fetches the CORS variant of every
# file and refuses to finish while any one of them differs from the tree.
#
# THIS FILE ONLY ADDRESSES ONE OF THE TWO CACHES, and knowing which is the whole trick:
#
#   Browser Cache TTL   what the visitor is told -- the `max-age` in the response. THIS file, when
#                       the zone is set to respect origin headers. Fixed 2026-09-21: the zone had
#                       been rewriting max-age=0 to max-age=300, and a Cache Rule now lets it pass.
#   Edge Cache TTL      how long Cloudflare's own edge keeps the object. NOT settable from here at
#                       all -- only a Cache Rule sets it -- and it is what actually decides whether
#                       a deploy is visible. Measured after the browser half was fixed:
#                       `cache-control: max-age=0, must-revalidate` with `cf-cache-status: HIT` and
#                       `age: 4142`. The browser is behaving perfectly and revalidating every time;
#                       the edge answers that revalidation from its own hours-old copy.
#
# So a rule that says "cache for a day" makes this WORSE, not better: it is the edge half, and a
# longer edge TTL is a longer lie. What this site wants is Edge TTL = Bypass, because Pages is
# already a global CDN and a second cache in front of it buys nothing and costs correctness.
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=0, must-revalidate
